  the journal Surveillance & Society\, funds small research activities in s
 urveillance studies\, including work on surveillance technologies\, data\,
  biometrics and AI-driven monitoring. Grants can cover costs such as trans
 cription\, participant payments\, travel\, equipment or conference fees.\n
 \nOrganisation: Surveillance Studies Network (SSN)\nLocation: Worldwide\, 
 with preference for researchers based in economically under-resourced regi
 ons (priority to UN-ranked Least Developed Countries). Applied by email\; 
 no travel required to apply.\nAward: Up to GBP 1\,500 per project\, plus a
  two-year SSN membership. The 2025-26 round made two awards. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Funds to be spent during the 2026-27 academic year\, by 
 5 January 2028.\n\nMore: https://surveillance-studies.net/honours/ssn-smal
